      "content": "Wait, did you just say \"core routed fracturing MDF material and suitable webs\"? I'm talking about a heavy structural Douglas Fir beam for a floor load, not building a piece of furniture or using MDF. That doesn't make sense for a structural load-bearing span. \n\nAlso, you mentioned the material properties can vary. Beyond just the grade, what should I be looking for when I actually inspect the timber on-site? I'm worried about finding some internal issues or structural inconsistencies once I start mounting the joists.",
